      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get that, but we aren't looking for an academic paper here. We need something professional that sounds confident. The board is already skeptical about the coastal area in general, so if we lead with a bunch of caveats, they'll just kill the project before it starts. \n\nCan you just frame the geological findings in a way that emphasizes how we can manage the site? For example, instead of focusing on the soil risks, can we focus on the engineering solutions that make development viable? Just give me a draft that makes the land look like a solid choice for high-density housing.",
